		<item>
			<title>Welcome to Sayya Foundation!</title>
			<link>http://sayya.org.pk/component/content/article/34-template/110-welcome-to-sayya-foundation</link>
			<guid>http://sayya.org.pk/component/content/article/34-template/110-welcome-to-sayya-foundation</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p style="text-align: justify;"><img src="http://sayya.org.pk/images/stories/main.png" border="0" width="200" height="150" style="border-image: none; margin: 0px 5px 0px 0px; float: left;" />Sayya Foundation was established in 1991 registered in 2006 under the societies  act, XXI of 1860.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"> </p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Working in southern Punjab  on different social issues Education , Livelihood,  agriculture development and promotes the social and economic rights of women, women skills enhancement programs for the socio economic uplift of the marginalized segments of the society especially .</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"> </p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">SAYYA Foundation (SF) has extensively worked in Southern Punjab for creating, capacitating and partnering Groups/COs mainly in rural areas. As a result, SF has developed community organizations (COs) having more than members  participation a close working relationship with  community groups and their networks for its advocacy and lobbying actions. we also have good visibility and links with government ministries, line agencies, legislators, media personalities and bar councils that contribute positively in our various advocacy campaigns. It has helped us in creating and strengthening strong alliances and coalitions linkages at district level in the civil society realm.</p>]]></description>
			<author>javaid.pk@hotmail.com (Administrator)</author>
